  "body": "## What changed\n\nName the stock band around the part when a stock-source pocket-family operation refuses because the cutter cannot fit.\nThe reported reproduction now names the 2.000 mm minimum side width and the 3.000 mm tool.\nThe refusal also names stock to leave per wall and suggests a smaller tool, wider stock, or a 2D Contour.\nTrue pockets keep their existing refusal, with a part selection and with the stock as the source.\nCurved bands receive advice without an invented width.\nGeneration still refuses the same job and emits no path.\n\nThe band message applies only when the area surrounds kept material.\nA piece of the stock-minus-part region is a band when its outer loop is a loop of the stock outline, and material stands inside that loop.\nA closed pocket and a pocket around an island have part walls as their boundary. They keep the pocket refusal.\nA strip of stock beside a part that is flush with the other stock sides also keeps the pocket refusal.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe generator reports a generic pocket error before the successful-path band note can run.\nThe app holds the stock-source context needed to explain that error.\n\n## Tests\n\nFinal head: `0d316a6dc57c22d007e08e89c13828e1b5643156`.\nGate base: current `upstream/main` at `cd0222d9cceb5e6f831a13071b93f1d083c3f10e`.\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test narrow_band` passed all ten tests.\nThe eight tests of this PR are:\n\n- `a_stock_source_adaptive_refusal_names_the_band_width_and_a_fix`\n- `a_stock_band_refusal_names_stock_to_leave`\n- `a_stock_band_refusal_measures_the_controlled_boundary`\n- `a_part_source_narrow_pocket_keeps_its_own_refusal`\n- `a_stock_source_closed_pocket_keeps_its_own_refusal` (review round 1)\n- `a_stock_source_pocket_around_an_island_keeps_its_own_refusal` (review round 1)\n- `a_stock_band_refusal_uses_document_inches`\n- `a_curved_stock_band_refusal_does_not_invent_a_rectangular_width`\n\nPin proof, first round: the primary pin failed on unchanged upstream code before the fix.\nRestoring upstream's exact `run_job.rs` made all five diagnostic pins fail.\n\nPin proof, review round 1:\n\n- Mutation A disabled the `surrounds_kept_material` guard. The two new controls failed. The other eight tests passed.\n- Mutation B kept the guard and disabled only its stock-outline test. `a_stock_source_pocket_around_an_island_keeps_its_own_refusal` failed. The other nine tests passed.\n- The restored fix passed all ten tests.\n\nResults on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 148 steps passed, zero failed, zero stalled, 15.5 minutes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 62 steps passed, zero failed, zero stalled, 20.9 minutes.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: one step passed, zero failed.\n\nEffort: medium.\nNo escalation.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe catalog suite ran and passed on the final head before this result was recorded.\nThe quick gate's `adaptive_trochoid` posted-program golden checks also passed.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- '*.nc' '*.cl' examples/catalog` produced no changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo GUI or physical controller run.\nThe diagnostic does not infer numeric widths for arbitrary band shapes.\nNo test covers a tilted (3+2) stock-source band. The guard reads the stock facets in the frame of the region there.\nNo test covers the strip beside a flush part. It has no hole, so the guard keeps the pocket refusal.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found in the three Step 2 file checks.\nThe branch starts at `upstream/main` commit `3c68dcaf2` and is not stacked.\nThe branch merges cleanly with the current `upstream/main`.\n\nChangelog: Explain narrow stock-band refusals with the band width, tool size, stock to leave, and corrective advice.\n\nFixes #3791\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
